BEHAVIOR string-to-bytes

DESCRIPTION
  Translates a self-describing string into a raw byte buffer plus an explicit
  length. A socket sends bytes, not strings, so to send a string literal you
  translate it here first, then pass the bytes + length to send.

CONTRACT
  INPUT text string
  OUTPUT data bytes 65536
  OUTPUT length int 8
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH a2e66e29

NATIVE
